#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:16
msgid "Current implementation and planned integration"
msgstr "Current implementation and planned integration"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:18
msgid ""
"The current implementation has common C wrappers and a Native provider. The "
"wrappers validate a face and dispatch through its immutable operations table"
" to its context. Native instances share two readonly operations tables, one "
"per device class, and retain independent state. There is no heap, registry, "
"hidden worker, request queue or mandatory OS adapter."
msgstr ""
"The current implementation has common C wrappers and a Native provider. The "
"wrappers validate a face and dispatch through its immutable operations table"
" to its context. Native instances share two readonly operations tables, one "
"per device class, and retain independent state. There is no heap, registry, "
"hidden worker, request queue or mandatory OS adapter."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:20
msgid ""
"Construction is an internal integration boundary. Generated Platform "
"preparation constructs fresh owner storage once, copies the selected Core "
"clock face without invoking its time reader, and opens admission. Later "
"starts of the constructed owner use explicit private reopen. External "
"products use public and generated headers, not private provider "
"constructors. The RTC initially stays unset until an explicit public set."
msgstr ""
"Construction is an internal integration boundary. Generated Platform "
"preparation constructs fresh owner storage once, copies the selected Core "
"clock face without invoking its time reader, and opens admission. Later "
"starts of the constructed owner use explicit private reopen. External "
"products use public and generated headers, not private provider "
"constructors. The RTC initially stays unset until an explicit public set."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:22
msgid ""
"Explicit private reopen and ordinary typed configuration assembly are "
"implemented for the selected Native host models. Private reopen changes the "
"owner incarnation after actual withdrawal and external joins instead of "
"reconstructing storage. H743 and U575 RTC/LPTIM adaptation remains a future "
"target with separate hardware contracts and evidence."
msgstr ""
"Explicit private reopen and ordinary typed configuration assembly are "
"implemented for the selected Native host models. Private reopen changes the "
"owner incarnation after actual withdrawal and external joins instead of "
"reconstructing storage. H743 and U575 RTC/LPTIM adaptation remains a future "
"target with separate hardware contracts and evidence."

