#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:28
msgid "Three domains, three meanings"
msgstr "Three domains, three meanings"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:30
msgid ""
"Core deadlines are absolute monotonic microseconds read through the copied "
"`nx_clock_t` face. The original face descriptor may be copied, but its "
"context remains borrowed: assembly must preserve the entire context "
"lifetime, disjoint storage, finite monotonic readings and non-reentrant "
"access. A finite deadline expires when the observed Core time is greater "
"than or equal to it. `NX_DEADLINE_NEVER` avoids a deadline read; it does not"
" make the calendar or counter advance."
msgstr ""
"Core deadlines are absolute monotonic microseconds read through the copied "
"`nx_clock_t` face. The original face descriptor may be copied, but its "
"context remains borrowed: assembly must preserve the entire context "
"lifetime, disjoint storage, finite monotonic readings and non-reentrant "
"access. A finite deadline expires when the observed Core time is greater "
"than or equal to it. `NX_DEADLINE_NEVER` avoids a deadline read; it does not"
" make the calendar or counter advance."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:32
msgid ""
"RTC uses raw year `00..99`, month/day and 24-hour time without UTC, a "
"century, timezone or leap seconds. Leap years satisfy raw year modulo 4 "
"equals zero. Weekday is an independent `1..7` field. Natural `99 -> 00` "
"rollover advances the calendar without creating a new setting domain; an "
"explicit successful set advances the nonwrapping generation."
msgstr ""
"RTC uses raw year `00..99`, month/day and 24-hour time without UTC, a "
"century, timezone or leap seconds. Leap years satisfy raw year modulo 4 "
"equals zero. Weekday is an independent `1..7` field. Natural `99 -> 00` "
"rollover advances the calendar without creating a new setting domain; an "
"explicit successful set advances the nonwrapping generation."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:34
msgid ""
"An RTC alarm matches one future day-of-month/hour/minute/second pattern. It "
"has no month/year field or wildcard mask. A pattern already matching the "
"current second is rejected with `STATE`; the provider does not silently "
"interpret it as a later recurrence. The product owns UTC conversion, date "
"selection, synchronization, recurrence and authorization policy."
msgstr ""
"An RTC alarm matches one future day-of-month/hour/minute/second pattern. It "
"has no month/year field or wildcard mask. A pattern already matching the "
"current second is rejected with `STATE`; the provider does not silently "
"interpret it as a later recurrence. The product owns UTC conversion, date "
"selection, synchronization, recurrence and authorization policy."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:36
msgid ""
"LPTIM accepts one finite shot of `1..65536` ticks. Its positive `tick_hz` is"
" a fixed declared unit rate, not measured oscillator accuracy. The 16-bit "
"sample is modulo 65536: a complete 65536-tick shot can sample as zero. "
"Counter zero alone proves neither completion nor low-power continuity. Open "
"idle returns zero and `running=false`; closed public read/sample returns "
"`STATE` without changing output."
msgstr ""
"LPTIM accepts one finite shot of `1..65536` ticks. Its positive `tick_hz` is"
" a fixed declared unit rate, not measured oscillator accuracy. The 16-bit "
"sample is modulo 65536: a complete 65536-tick shot can sample as zero. "
"Counter zero alone proves neither completion nor low-power continuity. Open "
"idle returns zero and `running=false`; closed public read/sample returns "
"`STATE` without changing output."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:38
msgid ""
"RTC and LPTIM domains contain the owner address and a checked `uint64_t` "
"generation. They are separate types and are not Core deadline tokens. RTC "
"set, private reopen and completed LPTIM withdrawal invalidate older domains."
" Tokens compare identity without dereferencing it; they establish neither "
"authorization nor cross-boot identity. Retire every token and external "
"observer before ending or reusing owner storage."
msgstr ""
"RTC and LPTIM domains contain the owner address and a checked `uint64_t` "
"generation. They are separate types and are not Core deadline tokens. RTC "
"set, private reopen and completed LPTIM withdrawal invalidate older domains."
" Tokens compare identity without dereferencing it; they establish neither "
"authorization nor cross-boot identity. Retire every token and external "
"observer before ending or reusing owner storage."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:40
msgid ""
"Generation never wraps silently. A Native RTC set at `UINT64_MAX` returns "
"`EXHAUSTED`; a Native LPTIM submission at that limit refuses before "
"acceptance so a previously accepted shot can always perform its reserved "
"final generation increment. Exhaustion is not permission to reset a stopped "
"owner or abandon a loan."
msgstr ""
"Generation never wraps silently. A Native RTC set at `UINT64_MAX` returns "
"`EXHAUSTED`; a Native LPTIM submission at that limit refuses before "
"acceptance so a previously accepted shot can always perform its reserved "
"final generation increment. Exhaustion is not permission to reset a stopped "
"owner or abandon a loan."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:42
msgid "Who owns storage and execution"
msgstr "Who owns storage and execution"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:44
msgid ""
"One serialized, non-reentrant task executor owns all calls on an instance, "
"including reads, model controls and lifecycle. The face, operations table, "
"private owner and borrowed clock context outlive every accepted request and "
"any separate observer/control joins. No implicit cross-task lock or ISR "
"entry contract is provided. Products that need cross-task cancellation must "
"add explicit stable-slot/epoch control and joining outside this provider."
msgstr ""
"One serialized, non-reentrant task executor owns all calls on an instance, "
"including reads, model controls and lifecycle. The face, operations table, "
"private owner and borrowed clock context outlive every accepted request and "
"any separate observer/control joins. No implicit cross-task lock or ISR "
"entry contract is provided. Products that need cross-task cancellation must "
"add explicit stable-slot/epoch control and joining outside this provider."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:46
msgid ""
"The caller owns the complete request. Initialize its Core base before "
"preparing it; prepare only unborrowed `READY` or consumed `SETTLED` storage "
"after all joins. Preparation copies metadata and takes no loan. The request "
"and input/output spans must be aligned, nonwrapping and disjoint from known "
"protected objects. These checks are not a universal invalid-pointer or "
"memory-access oracle; assembly remains responsible for opaque context "
"extents and live mapped storage."
msgstr ""
"The caller owns the complete request. Initialize its Core base before "
"preparing it; prepare only unborrowed `READY` or consumed `SETTLED` storage "
"after all joins. Preparation copies metadata and takes no loan. The request "
"and input/output spans must be aligned, nonwrapping and disjoint from known "
"protected objects. These checks are not a universal invalid-pointer or "
"memory-access oracle; assembly remains responsible for opaque context "
"extents and live mapped storage."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:48
msgid ""
"Each instance accepts at most one request. Submission validates lifecycle, "
"idle state, the current domain and the class-specific range before reading a"
" finite deadline. `SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED; rejection retains no request or "
"source effects. A rejected request stays caller-owned. A missing optional "
"operations-table method returns `UNSUPPORTED`; malformed public inputs may "
"return `INVALID` before provider dispatch."
msgstr ""
"Each instance accepts at most one request. Submission validates lifecycle, "
"idle state, the current domain and the class-specific range before reading a"
" finite deadline. `SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED; rejection retains no request or "
"source effects. A rejected request stays caller-owned. A missing optional "
"operations-table method returns `UNSUPPORTED`; malformed public inputs may "
"return `INVALID` before provider dispatch."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:50
msgid ""
"After ACCEPTED the caller keeps every request byte live and immutable until "
"acquire-observed `SETTLED`, then consumes the result and joins any separate "
"controls or observers before reuse. Cancellation, expiry, stop, a failed "
"withdrawal or a sampled completion flag never revoke this loan."
msgstr ""
"After ACCEPTED the caller keeps every request byte live and immutable until "
"acquire-observed `SETTLED`, then consumes the result and joins any separate "
"controls or observers before reuse. Cancellation, expiry, stop, a failed "
"withdrawal or a sampled completion flag never revoke this loan."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:52
msgid "Source progression, terminal cause and final access"
msgstr "Source progression, terminal cause and final access"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:54
msgid ""
"Host model advancement changes source state only. RTC advancement is bounded"
" to `0..86400` seconds per call with at most one date carry; an initialized "
"calendar may advance while admission is closed. LPTIM advancement is bounded"
" to `0..65536` ticks and saturates at the shot limit; an unarmed source "
"accumulates nothing. These hooks neither read Core time nor touch or settle "
"requests. Setting or clearing the withdrawal hold also does not settle a "
"request."
msgstr ""
"Host model advancement changes source state only. RTC advancement is bounded"
" to `0..86400` seconds per call with at most one date carry; an initialized "
"calendar may advance while admission is closed. LPTIM advancement is bounded"
" to `0..65536` ticks and saturates at the shot limit; an unarmed source "
"accumulates nothing. These hooks neither read Core time nor touch or settle "
"requests. Setting or clearing the withdrawal hold also does not settle a "
"request."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:56
msgid ""
"Explicit public service observes the predicate and advances withdrawal. "
"Cancel and stop can call withdrawal directly, so they may settle immediately"
" when no hold remains; service is not the only final publisher. On first "
"service observation an expired finite deadline wins over a pending event. An"
" earlier cancel or stop may instead latch `CANCELLED`. Once latched, the "
"first terminal cause stays fixed while withdrawal waits."
msgstr ""
"Explicit public service observes the predicate and advances withdrawal. "
"Cancel and stop can call withdrawal directly, so they may settle immediately"
" when no hold remains; service is not the only final publisher. On first "
"service observation an expired finite deadline wins over a pending event. An"
" earlier cancel or stop may instead latch `CANCELLED`. Once latched, the "
"first terminal cause stays fixed while withdrawal waits."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:58
msgid ""
"If withdrawal is held, the request remains borrowed and `QUARANTINED`. "
"Cancel can return `SUCCESS` because cancellation was accepted while "
"service/stop returns `BUSY`. Removing a model hold only makes a later real "
"withdrawal possible; the executor must still call an appropriate public "
"service/cancel/stop operation. Keep the owner and request alive while that "
"work remains."
msgstr ""
"If withdrawal is held, the request remains borrowed and `QUARANTINED`. "
"Cancel can return `SUCCESS` because cancellation was accepted while "
"service/stop returns `BUSY`. Removing a model hold only makes a later real "
"withdrawal possible; the executor must still call an appropriate public "
"service/cancel/stop operation. Keep the owner and request alive while that "
"work remains."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:60
msgid ""
"Successful withdrawal first disables the source, clears pending state and "
"detaches the owner reference. LPTIM also records final tick progress and "
"advances its generation before publication. Only then does the provider "
"release-publish `SETTLED` as its last request access. RTC `transferred` is 1"
" for success and 0 otherwise. LPTIM `transferred` is the final observed tick"
" count, including ticks accrued while withdrawal was held; it is not frozen "
"when cancel/timeout first latches."
msgstr ""
"Successful withdrawal first disables the source, clears pending state and "
"detaches the owner reference. LPTIM also records final tick progress and "
"advances its generation before publication. Only then does the provider "
"release-publish `SETTLED` as its last request access. RTC `transferred` is 1"
" for success and 0 otherwise. LPTIM `transferred` is the final observed tick"
" count, including ticks accrued while withdrawal was held; it is not frozen "
"when cancel/timeout first latches."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:62
msgid ""
"Stop closes admission immediately, even when withdrawal returns `BUSY`. "
"Closed reads and submissions remain rejected, while service/cancel can still"
" drain the retained loan. A repeated clean stop is idempotent. Successful "
"stop does not end owner storage lifetime or waive external joins. Reopening "
"is a separate explicit private lifecycle operation, not a side effect of "
"lookup, model advancement or a repeated constructor."
msgstr ""
"Stop closes admission immediately, even when withdrawal returns `BUSY`. "
"Closed reads and submissions remain rejected, while service/cancel can still"
" drain the retained loan. A repeated clean stop is idempotent. Successful "
"stop does not end owner storage lifetime or waive external joins. Reopening "
"is a separate explicit private lifecycle operation, not a side effect of "
"lookup, model advancement or a repeated constructor."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:64
msgid "Explicit private reopen preserves identity and responsibility"
msgstr "Explicit private reopen preserves identity and responsibility"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:66
msgid ""
"A constructor is valid once per owner storage lifetime. The internal "
"`nx_native_rtc_start` and `nx_native_lptim_start` operations reopen that "
"same stable owner; they are not public application SDK APIs. They require a "
"valid constructed, closed owner with no active request, armed source, "
"pending event or terminal responsibility. The caller must also prove that "
"external controls and observers have joined; inspecting owner fields cannot "
"establish those external joins."
msgstr ""
"A constructor is valid once per owner storage lifetime. The internal "
"`nx_native_rtc_start` and `nx_native_lptim_start` operations reopen that "
"same stable owner; they are not public application SDK APIs. They require a "
"valid constructed, closed owner with no active request, armed source, "
"pending event or terminal responsibility. The caller must also prove that "
"external controls and observers have joined; inspecting owner fields cannot "
"establish those external joins."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:68
msgid ""
"After full-span validation, retained request/source responsibility takes "
"`BUSY` priority over unconstructed/already-open `STATE`. A closed joined "
"owner at `UINT64_MAX` returns `NX_ERROR_EXHAUSTED`. Every rejection "
"preserves all owner bytes, source facts, fault state, clock and generation. "
"Start is not idempotent: a clean already-open owner returns `STATE`. A held "
"closed loan remains borrowed and `QUARANTINED`; neither start nor repeated "
"construction can revoke it."
msgstr ""
"After full-span validation, retained request/source responsibility takes "
"`BUSY` priority over unconstructed/already-open `STATE`. A closed joined "
"owner at `UINT64_MAX` returns `NX_ERROR_EXHAUSTED`. Every rejection "
"preserves all owner bytes, source facts, fault state, clock and generation. "
"Start is not idempotent: a clean already-open owner returns `STATE`. A held "
"closed loan remains borrowed and `QUARANTINED`; neither start nor repeated "
"construction can revoke it."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:70
msgid ""
"On success private start checks generation capacity, increments the "
"generation, then opens admission. It reads no Core time, advances no source,"
" reconstructs nothing and adds no state field or owner pool. It preserves "
"the RTC set/unset state and calendar, LPTIM fixed `tick_hz`, copied clock "
"binding and external withdrawal hold. A hold flag on an otherwise idle "
"joined owner is an external fault, not an active loan; reopening preserves "
"it rather than silently clearing it."
msgstr ""
"On success private start checks generation capacity, increments the "
"generation, then opens admission. It reads no Core time, advances no source,"
" reconstructs nothing and adds no state field or owner pool. It preserves "
"the RTC set/unset state and calendar, LPTIM fixed `tick_hz`, copied clock "
"binding and external withdrawal hold. A hold flag on an otherwise idle "
"joined owner is an external fault, not an active loan; reopening preserves "
"it rather than silently clearing it."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:72
msgid ""
"The final permitted reopen can move `UINT64_MAX - 1` to `UINT64_MAX`; after "
"a later clean stop another reopen is exhausted. Old externally held `READY` "
"domains remain stale and reject submission unchanged. No wrap, reset-to-one "
"or implicit fresh construction repairs exhaustion. Model source progression "
"and result consumption remain separate from this lifecycle transition."
msgstr ""
"The final permitted reopen can move `UINT64_MAX - 1` to `UINT64_MAX`; after "
"a later clean stop another reopen is exhausted. Old externally held `READY` "
"domains remain stale and reject submission unchanged. No wrap, reset-to-one "
"or implicit fresh construction repairs exhaustion. Model source progression "
"and result consumption remain separate from this lifecycle transition."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:74
msgid "Typed assembly uses the existing configuration path"
msgstr "Typed assembly uses the existing configuration path"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:76
msgid ""
"The maintained pair fixture below is a complete Native assembly. Ordinary "
"`[rtc.name]` and `[lptim.name]` sections resolve through the existing "
"immutable `ControllerIR -> provider -> factory` path. `calendar-alarm` has "
"no date or timezone option; `counter16-oneshot` requires an explicit "
"positive `uint32_t` `tick_hz`. Unknown policy/IRQ fields and duplicate "
"controller claims are rejected rather than repaired."
msgstr ""
"The maintained pair fixture below is a complete Native assembly. Ordinary "
"`[rtc.name]` and `[lptim.name]` sections resolve through the existing "
"immutable `ControllerIR -> provider -> factory` path. `calendar-alarm` has "
"no date or timezone option; `counter16-oneshot` requires an explicit "
"positive `uint32_t` `tick_hz`. Unknown policy/IRQ fields and duplicate "
"controller claims are rejected rather than repaired."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:82
msgid ""
"Native host-model facts expose RTC0/RTC1 and LPTIM0/LPTIM1 without pins or "
"IRQ routes. Two software RTC instances exercise isolation; they do not "
"assert two physical RTC peripherals. The generator emits only selected "
"static state, readonly faces and pure typed lookup. The selected shared "
"deadline adapter reads `nx_time_now_us()` without advancing any RTC/LPTIM "
"source. An empty assembly emits no selected RTC/LPTIM state or that adapter."
msgstr ""
"Native host-model facts expose RTC0/RTC1 and LPTIM0/LPTIM1 without pins or "
"IRQ routes. Two software RTC instances exercise isolation; they do not "
"assert two physical RTC peripherals. The generator emits only selected "
"static state, readonly faces and pure typed lookup. The selected shared "
"deadline adapter reads `nx_time_now_us()` without advancing any RTC/LPTIM "
"source. An empty assembly emits no selected RTC/LPTIM state or that adapter."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:84
msgid "Public and generated entry points"
msgstr "Public and generated entry points"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:86
msgid ""
"Use `nexus_factory.h` to obtain `nx_factory_rtc(id)` or "
"`nx_factory_lptim(id)`. IDs belong to the selected assembly and class; "
"invalid/unselected IDs return NULL. Faces and shared operations tables exist"
" before startup, but RTC read and LPTIM sample reject closed/unconstructed "
"use. Lookup neither constructs an owner nor reads a clock."
msgstr ""
"Use `nexus_factory.h` to obtain `nx_factory_rtc(id)` or "
"`nx_factory_lptim(id)`. IDs belong to the selected assembly and class; "
"invalid/unselected IDs return NULL. Faces and shared operations tables exist"
" before startup, but RTC read and LPTIM sample reject closed/unconstructed "
"use. Lookup neither constructs an owner nor reads a clock."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:88
msgid ""
"The external lifecycle owner calls `nx_platform_start()` and checks "
"`primary`, `cleanup` and `remaining_effects`. It then explicitly sets the "
"RTC if needed, copies a current domain, prepares caller-owned requests and "
"submits through public ports. It drives the required model source and public"
" service separately. Startup creates no scheduler, and Core-time advancement"
" does not advance a calendar or finite shot."
msgstr ""
"The external lifecycle owner calls `nx_platform_start()` and checks "
"`primary`, `cleanup` and `remaining_effects`. It then explicitly sets the "
"RTC if needed, copies a current domain, prepares caller-owned requests and "
"submits through public ports. It drives the required model source and public"
" service separately. Startup creates no scheduler, and Core-time advancement"
" does not advance a calendar or finite shot."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:90
msgid ""
"If `nx_platform_stop()` returns `BUSY`, retain every borrowed request and "
"its owner, drive real withdrawal, consume final results and join external "
"users before retrying stop. Complete Platform shutdown before another start;"
" it does not silently reconstruct or reopen an unfinished stop. The [pair "
"consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/native-time-pair.c)"
" and [empty consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/native-time-"
"empty.c) are maintained public/generated host verification programs, not "
"hardware application examples."
msgstr ""
"If `nx_platform_stop()` returns `BUSY`, retain every borrowed request and "
"its owner, drive real withdrawal, consume final results and join external "
"users before retrying stop. Complete Platform shutdown before another start;"
" it does not silently reconstruct or reopen an unfinished stop. The [pair "
"consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/native-time-pair.c)"
" and [empty consumer](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/cmake/package/verification/io_evolution/consumers/native-time-"
"empty.c) are maintained public/generated host verification programs, not "
"hardware application examples."

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:92
msgid "Costs and verification boundary"
msgstr "Costs and verification boundary"

#: ../../../nexus-io36-native-20261018/docs/explanation/rtc-lptim.md:94
msgid ""
"The public face contains two pointers; per-instance state contains the "
"copied clock face, domain and class-specific calendar/counter state. One "
"request is retained at a time. RTC model work is bounded without a per-"
"second loop; LPTIM uses bounded saturating arithmetic. This structure avoids"
" dynamic allocation and queue capacity costs, but it does not establish a "
"byte budget, stack bound, WCET, oscillator accuracy or MCU power result. "
"Measure those against the actual selected build and hardware."
msgstr ""
"The public face contains two pointers; per-instance state contains the "
"copied clock face, domain and class-specific calendar/counter state. One "
"request is retained at a time. RTC model work is bounded without a per-"
"second loop; LPTIM uses bounded saturating arithmetic. This structure avoids"
" dynamic allocation and queue capacity costs, but it does not establish a "
"byte budget, stack bound, WCET, oscillator accuracy or MCU power result. "
"Measure those against the actual selected build and hardware."

